{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc","id":1196730,"title":"Alucard gets his grubby hands on AotC!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-17T23:38:06-07:00","id":1196730,"title":"Alucard gets his grubby hands on AotC!","content":"Any veterans of these forums might have noticed a sort-of hiatus on my part, at the end of last year. It was for a number of reasons; times were stressful, my Okeanos game was on break, I was depressed, my sister was wanting to start a Shadowrun game, and\u2026<br /> <br /> Truth be told, when <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> came out, I simply couldn't afford it. And I didn't want to spoil anything for myself, yet every day I was on these forums, my temptation to start reading the AotC thread was growing. <br /> <br /> But thanks to a very generous friend of mine, I now have a copy, and, well\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Holy shit</i>, you guys. I love this book. Thanks to everyone who took part in making it! The writing is evocative, the art is gorgeous, the Evocations are solid. There isn't a single Artifact in the book that I didn't like! Just reading it, I wanted to get into Exalted again, and in fact, <i>I am getting into Exalted again</i>.<br /> <br /> The guy who bought the book for me has volunteered to run a game, so a couple of friends and I will be playing scavenger lords, <i>and I fucking call dibs on Distaff</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks again, Devs, writers, illustrators, editors. I can't thank you enough. Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar229_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"229\" data-vbnamecard=\"229\">Stephen Lea Sheppard</a>; thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a>; thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1120_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1120\" data-vbnamecard=\"1120\">Eric Minton</a>; thanks, <i>everyone</i>.<br /> <br /> (And don't worry, my in-depth analysis will follow; I'll probably have to rest first though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-18-2018, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T10:21:55-07:00","id":1196845,"title":"","content":"The title made me think of Attack of the Clones due to the overlap in the Acronym use.<br /> Good to see you're enjoying it so far. I like the versatility of the book myself.<br /> The question I guess is have you had any ideas from reading it that you want to share so far?<br /> <br /> Hope you have fun with the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T10:59:00-07:00","id":1196855,"title":"","content":"What parts of Distaff enthuse you the most?<br /> <br /> Myself, I like the Evocations that enhance grapples, crafting actions, and medical treatments. I think those would be great for a pair of moonsilver weaver\u2019s gloves, especially with other Evocations that produce silk rope and rope-weapons: bolas, flails, lassos, nets, trampolines, web-walls and sticky web-traps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T21:38:24-07:00","id":1197028,"title":"","content":"<b>Courante and Galliard</b><br /> <br /> Right away I was excited; paired artifacts, but used between two users? Very interesting concept. I like that they start out with different Evocations that blend together; I had considered that for a pair of twin blades for Misu in my Okeanos game, but hadn't quite gotten there yet. I might have to crib from this. I like the anima teleportation, and the fusion effect at the end is just as glorious as I'd expect. <br /> <br /> <b>The Distaff</b> <br /> <br /> Fun story to it, <i>and</i> a great reminder of how these storied weapons don't just unlock powers; they <i>evolve</i> with their user. I must admit that the Evocations weren't what made me jump at this quite so much as the imagery. This may be the one where I don't <i>want</i> to unlock its capstone, because it's perfect the way it is. <br /> <br /> <b>Fist of Titans</b><br /> <br /> Right away I was intent on dissecting this one for bits to pilfer; it's a destructive bludgeoning weapon, and I know I've been lax in developing Evocations that grab the attention of my players for their artifacts. But even as I was trying to work my way between the fingers of this artifact to get at the core, I found I had to contend with the sheer unstoppable force of smashing that I would release on my game. I don't think I'm ready for this one.<br /> <br /> Yet. But man is it awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-19-2018, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T21:54:03-07:00","id":1197037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1196855#post1196855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What parts of Distaff enthuse you the most?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability to extrude silk from it, of any color. The way the Distaff makes your existing Charms more effective. The fact that it's named &quot;the Distaff,&quot; <i>and it looks and functions as a distaff.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1196855#post1196855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think those would be great for a pair of moonsilver weaver\u2019s gloves\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I might sound stupid for asking, but do weavers wear gloves? I Googled the phrase &quot;Weaver's gloves,&quot; and the first half-dozen or so results were all instances of the phrase being used in this RPG or that RPG, leaving me wondering if they're intended to be &quot;Weaver's gloves&quot; in the sense of being the gloves of someone who weaves, versus being the gloves of someone named Weaver.<br /> <br /> Regardless, though, I don't find myself agreeing with your point, because the Distaff replicates the look <i>and function</i> of a distaff: it holds the material for your spinning. If a weaver wears gloves, it's presumably to protect their hands while they're working, right? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1196855#post1196855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026especially with other Evocations that produce silk rope and rope-weapons: bolas, flails, lassos, nets, trampolines, web-walls and sticky web-traps.</div> </div> </div> </div>This comes off to me as something of an Air-Breathing Mermaid; you can make all sorts of things via Craftsman Needs No Tools, many in mere seconds due to the simplicity of the intended craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-19-2018, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:55:15-07:00","id":1197119,"title":"","content":"They use thimbles, more often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:56:16-07:00","id":1197149,"title":"","content":"I meant that the gloves would let you make silk-ropes reflexively, like Spider-Man. Webshooters.<br /> <br /> Also, my apologies, but I just threw the phrase \u201cweavers gloves\u201d out there from the idea of a weaver wearing gloves that simply produced silk from the gloves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:35:08-07:00","id":1197164,"title":"","content":"Bracers of silken tethering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T07:20:53-07:00","id":1197176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197149#post1197149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that the gloves would let you make silk-ropes reflexively, like Spider-Man. Webshooters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just say so next time, lol. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197149#post1197149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, my apologies, but I just threw the phrase \u201cweavers gloves\u201d out there from the idea of a weaver wearing gloves that simply produced silk from the gloves.</div> </div> </div> </div>No big. That said, I still think I prefer Distaff in its presented shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T07:51:02-07:00","id":1197192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197149#post1197149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that the gloves would let you make silk-ropes reflexively, like Spider-Man. Webshooters.<br /> <br /> Also, my apologies, but I just threw the phrase \u201cweavers gloves\u201d out there from the idea of a weaver wearing gloves that simply produced silk from the gloves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remind me of <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/b__/images/8/8e/ExcellionWire.png/revision/latest?cb=20111212090741&amp;path-prefix=blackcat\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>from Black Cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:18:01-07:00","id":1197201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc#post1196730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Truth be told, when <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> came out, I simply couldn't afford it. And I didn't want to spoil anything for myself, yet every day I was on these forums, my temptation to start reading the AotC thread was growing.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bMakes sense; I was the same with Masters of Jade.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bAlthough that was a case in which the Liminal Exalted were first spoiled for me by somebody bringing them up on a thread in Off-Topic of all places.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-19-2018, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:47:44-07:00","id":1197214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1196845#post1196845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title made me think of Attack of the Clones due to the overlap in the Acronym use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't <i>brag</i> about getting my hands on <i>Attack of the Clones</i>. That film is a hot potato. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good to see you're enjoying it so far. I like the versatility of the book myself. </div> </div> </div>Easily my favorite part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The question I guess is have you had any ideas from reading it that you want to share so far? </div> </div> </div>One of my friends is going to run a game for us; I'm playing a sorcerous scavenger lord who Exalted as a Twilight when he discovered the true history of the silk-wrapped sword he found. He grew up in Great Forks, where he spent a year as a spider as punishment for breaking into a god's occult library.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hope you have fun with the game. </div> </div> </div>I will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197201#post1197201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bMakes sense; I was the same with Masters of Jade.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bAlthough that was a case in which the Liminal Exalted were first spoiled for me by somebody bringing them up on a thread in Off-Topic of all places.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, same for me but Karvara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-19-2018, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:12:54-07:00","id":1197229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197028#post1197028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Distaff</b><br /> <br /> Fun story to it, <i>and</i> a great reminder of how these storied weapons don't just unlock powers; they <i>evolve</i> with their user. I must admit that the Evocations weren't what made me jump at this quite so much as the imagery. This may be the one where I don't <i>want</i> to unlock its capstone, because it's perfect the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197037#post1197037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ability to extrude silk from it, of any color. The way the Distaff makes your existing Charms more effective. The fact that it's named &quot;the Distaff,&quot; <i>and it looks and functions as a distaff.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> The team <i>certainly </i>exercised their creativity and gave some <i>great </i>examples of thinking outside the box. What is the Distaff? It is a medium weapon with tags that, don't quite match up with anything presented in the core, <i>but totally</i> make sense for it. A nice example of using the tag toolkit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:31:01-07:00","id":1197235,"title":"","content":"What do you think about Frost-Thorn Knuckles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:34:04-07:00","id":1197237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197235#post1197235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about Frost-Thorn Knuckles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just hold on, I'm running some errands today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:36:50-07:00","id":1197239,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to seeing what you think of the new warstrider rules, but those are waaaaaay at the back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T14:48:59-07:00","id":1197339,"title":"","content":"I think they're pretty awesome, my Night Caste has God-Speed Vanguard. Sadly I haven't battled any giant monsters yet, but we're probably going up against a Realm legion in the next game or two, so maybe I'll get to fight a Jade warstrider!<br /> <br /> I'm sure Alucard will enjoy them too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T16:37:28-07:00","id":1197384,"title":"","content":"Just got Arms of the Chosen too, still coming and going from chapter one and making notes along the way.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the thing that most got my attention is that Need-Fire <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pergola\" target=\"_blank\">Pergola</a>, going by its descrpitive name if nothing else, should have not only a dozen city-sized columns of simmering prismatic flame but half as many <b>crossbeams </b>of the same... now that's a sight and quite the place to mess with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T21:45:00-07:00","id":1197483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197229#post1197229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The team <i>certainly </i>exercised their creativity and gave some <i>great </i>examples of thinking outside the box. What is the Distaff? It is a medium weapon with tags that, don't quite match up with anything presented in the core, <i>but totally</i> make sense for it. A nice example of using the tag toolkit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also liked Distaff's origin story. Was she a Solar? Was she a Lunar? Was she just some weird individual with a magic knife-sword-silk-thingy? Who knows? Reads like something that'd of been at home in Flat Earth too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:57:34-07:00","id":1197535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197235#post1197235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about Frost-Thorn Knuckles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm ready now.<br /> <br /> <b>Frost-Thorn Knuckles</b><br /> <br /> First off, Orphan-Maker is a kick-ass name. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Moreover, I like what this suggests about the Silver Pact! <br /> <br /> I fear for the PCs who take Lace of Thorn's offer. <br /> <br /> <b>Hawk Star's Jess</b><br /> <br /> Pure fun. I like that it could plausibly find its way into the hands of any Sidereal. Doom mechanic is both exciting and accurately-named. Makes me wonder how big the Gigantes of Dis are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <b>Heartsong</b> <br /> <br /> The ranged weapons in this book really shine. Two Fair Folk's passions pulsing through the jade core of a powerbow? My only complaint is that I wanted to do something similar with a pair of hookswords for Misu, and now I'll look like I'm ripping you guys off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:23:46-07:00","id":1198738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197239#post1197239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to seeing what you think of the new warstrider rules, but those are waaaaaay at the back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Words cannot contain my enthusiasm for them. But it'll have to wait, my apologies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197339#post1197339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're pretty awesome, my Night Caste has God-Speed Vanguard. Sadly I haven't battled any giant monsters yet\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of monster would grant you a warstrider, but no kaiju to slay?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197339#post1197339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026but we're probably going up against a Realm legion in the next game or two, so maybe I'll get to fight a Jade warstrider!</div> </div> </div> </div>Have someone with a dreamstone standing by to record the battle. For posterity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Alternatively, sell tickets, or start a betting pool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1197339#post1197339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure Alucard will enjoy them too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much did.<br /> <br /> <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> is rather unlike the RPG supplements I'm used to, where you have to sift through the crap to find one or two sparkling emeralds; <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> is a basket brimming with gems. And every time I thought I'd found my favorite, I had to revise my position as I read on and encountered Five Edicts Dominion, or when I flipped back and remembered how cool Asphodel was.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:46:48-07:00","id":1198748,"title":"","content":"<b>Heaven and Earth Gauntlets</b><br /> <br /> Poor Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Love how many of these Artifacts have been made by non-Solars. The classic reference to Greek myth in the text of Legend-Forging Blow made me smile. I also find it clever, how the reset conditions of the capstone Charms of so many of these Artifacts encourage groups toward telling certain stories.<br /> <br /> <b>Irenio's Bell</b> <br /> <br /> I fuckin' love this game. If I was playing D&amp;D, and the party defeated a demon prince, and I said, &quot;I want to take his temple bell and make a magic shield out of it, along with the broken pieces of my magic sword,&quot; the DM and the other players would probably spend the next twenty minutes trying to come up with twenty ways to persuade me to &quot;stop being ridiculous.&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead we have a game where doing so results in a brassy orichalcum defensive weapon that builds destructive resonance as it is hit in combat, until you can channel its unholy power to call up a demon to fight by your side.<br /> <br /> <b>Rainwalker</b><br /> <br /> Razor Parasol? Razor Parasol. B)<br /> <br /> The description of this artifact puts a very vivid image in my head. I wonder what the practical difference is between using a raksha's grace to make an artifact, versus using the raksha itself.<br /> <br /> I doubt that razor parasols are common enough in Creation to call for a martial arts style that has such as a form weapon\u2026 that doesn't stop me wanting it, though. <br /> <br /> <b>Razor Dancer and Wise Steel</b> <br /> <br /> I like that the heroes trapped in the blades are not gendered <i>and</i> don't have their splat types given; they could conceivably be anything. I also liked contrasting these weapons to Courante and Galliard; this pair of weapons has yet to become very storied, and uses Form-type Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-23-2018, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T23:20:23-07:00","id":1199604,"title":"","content":"<b>Summer Thunder</b><br /> <br /> This is another one of those &quot;Fuck yeah, Exalted&quot; items. A bow, strung with the god of horses' mane, that produces mounted archers from its arrows? I love it; one of my players, he was flipping through the book, and as soon as he saw this item, he wanted to <i>play</i> a character <i>with</i> this item.<br /> <br /> <b>Sun's Brush</b><br /> <br /> Gods in love, jealous paramours, a secret order of librarians, and a magic calligraphy spear? I might have to raise my standards; try as I might to stay on my feet, y'all keep bowling me over.<br /> <br /> I <i>did</i> have to reread a bit, as I was confused as to the reasoning behind it permitting decisive attacks in the place of foe-scribing gambits; that was until I recalled that some earlier Evocations <i>only</i> worked with foe-scribing. But now you can set those guys <i>on fire</i>. Cool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>The Tusk of Galaech-Ma</b><br /> <br /> This is a weapon with personality. I wonder how much easier of a time Wander would have had against the Colossi with this bad boy. And again, we see a weapon crafted by a non-Solar and yet still totally badass. I approve. <br /> <br /> I wonder how its Evocations might be different in the hands of another kind of Exalt, though. Would the Lunar Charmset be compatible enough to not require overmuch structural difference? Intriguing, to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T05:53:57-07:00","id":1199677,"title":"","content":"With non-orichalcum weapons, the writers seem to have stuck with writing Evocations derived from Solar Charms that most likely have approximations in the Charmsets of the associated Exalted.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted have equal, full resonance with all artifacts, but that doesn\u2019t mean that all Solar Charms always combine with every possible Evocation.<br /> <br /> Looking to Volcano Cutter, you could easily build something from Magma Burial and Leaping Tiger Attack or Thunderbolt Attack Prana, but there aren\u2019t many Solar Charms that would seem to improve Caldera Reconfiguration Stance or Pyroclastic Holocaust. But Dragon-Blooded have Charms like Dragon Vortex Attack, which might. <br /> <br /> But orichalcum Evocations should pretty much always synergize with Solar Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:23:26-07:00","id":1199691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1199604#post1199604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as soon as he saw this item, he wanted to <i>play</i> a character <i>with</i> this item.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the big triumph of the book, I think; items that can inspire characters built around them.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot to knock the ones given in the corebook, mind.<br /> <br /> Conversely, if Eska's write-up is anything to go by*, there's also a good opportunity in characterising a figure by mentioning the cues that they give to the powers of their weapons. Even if it's just a line, it will be nice for them to be more than a fancy name.<br /> <br /> \u200b* I don't know if any of the Dragon Blooded Adversaries have Artifact weapons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:26:06-07:00","id":1199694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1199691#post1199691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b* I don't know if any of the Dragon Blooded Adversaries have Artifact weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of them, Ragara Feria, does. Her weapon gives some minor advantages that seem very in line with her charms and playstyle (Fire Aspect Captain).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:38:49-07:00","id":1199699,"title":"","content":"None of the QCs I've seen have more than a few basic evocations listed. If you nick their stuff you're gonna have to stat up a lot of it yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T09:11:06-07:00","id":1199730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1199694#post1199694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of them, Ragara Feria, does. Her weapon gives some minor advantages that seem very in line with her charms and playstyle (Fire Aspect Captain).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember if it's literally Mistweaver or just very remiscent of it....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:27:59-07:00","id":1199753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1199691#post1199691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the big triumph of the book, I think; items that can inspire characters built around them.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot to knock the ones given in the corebook, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Adorei's certainly no chopped liver; it's just that, I think, no one wants to be the one to cause the poor girl to burn out. <br /> <br /> <b>Asphodel</b><br /> <br /> In the <i>very first sentence</i>, we get a nice little point about how even during the First Age, a genius Solar artisan still found the insight of a mortal to be something worth preserving. Well, &quot;mortal,&quot; anyway, given that the guy was a sorcerer. Still cool. I love that the mace has its own world hidden inside. <br /> <br /> The illustration is fun, too. Perfect Soul seems a bit weirded out; I imagine I would be, too.<br /> <br /> Love the descriptions. I'm assuming that like &quot;Creature of Darkness,&quot; &quot;Undead&quot; is one of those non-exhaustive categories where the ST is assumed to have final say over what falls under its umbrella?<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Branch</b><br /> <br /> This one is also fun; a green jade weapon that unlocks fire-themed Evocations through housing a fiery hearthstone, via the myth-logic of fiery oaths and of it being, well, a burning branch. And it can even damage artifacts! Sounds like I should keep those repair Charms handy, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Flying Silver Dream</b> <br /> <br /> It's a continuation of the same story from Courante and Galliard, and a reminder that even something as potent as an artifact might see reason to be put aside. Irenio gets a name-drop here as well. I like how the weapon basically becomes a separate combatant; the older editions' FSD didn't seem to convey that the way this one does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T18:49:09-07:00","id":1203230,"title":"","content":"Are you going to keep going? I want to read more!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T19:16:26-07:00","id":1203244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1203230#post1203230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you going to keep going? I want to read more!</div> </div> </div> </div> I absolutely intend to; as I am sure you're aware, though, the presence of certain other things lately has distracted me a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll get right back to it ASAP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T08:57:13-07:00","id":1203422,"title":"","content":"Onward!<br /> <br /> <b>Gnomon</b> <br /> <br /> I was jazzed about this one as far back as the preview, and my opinion on it hasn't much changed; it's really cool to see the sort of sneaky mischief a Night Caste can get up to. I also love the Evocations; stopping time and messing with people is just really cool.<br /> <br /> I wonder what sort of stories of Seven-Finger Wu Anys Syn shared with Serafina.<br /> <br /> <b>Mistweaver</b><br /> <br /> Much like the Distaff, the sheer stuff you can do with this weapon before you even use an Evocation makes it worthwhile; not only are your senses not impeded by water in any form, you can even hack mist and the like out of the way so your buddies can see too!<br /> <br /> I can see that a Night Caste who gets the Stealth Charms that get more powerful as he remains concealed in combat will be a <b>very</b> dangerous opponent it he's permitted to get his hands on this weapon.<br /> <br /> *reads Death in the Mist*<br /> <br /> A <b><i>super</i></b> dangerous opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmare Shard</b><br /> <br /> Okay, I thought it would be <i>at least</i> two pages before I came across a name as metal as &quot;Death in the Mist.&quot; I'm happy to say I was wrong.<br /> <br /> And another fun story hook handed to me on a silver platter. Ex3 authors, you've gone a long way to making STing Exalted easier!<br /> <br /> I <i>know</i> this weapon is a boomerang, but it took until Dream-Rending Strike for my mind's eye to stop seeing it as a sword. I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> I thought I was going to stop there, but then I remembered what came next\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Sekhem</b><br /> <br /> Glad I've already read <i>Lord of Light</i> so I can catch the reference, there! I love this weapon. It really sizzles! <br /> <br /> Okay, okay, I'll try not to do puns like that. But I make no promises.<br /> <br /> No, but seriously, I love that the consequence of making a weapon burn hot enough to damage things immune to fire is that <i>it burns too hot to be immune to itself</i>. <br /> <br /> The illustration is great, for that matter. It matches perfectly the one in my head. <br /> <br /> Okay, that's it for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T07:34:30-07:00","id":1203823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1203422#post1203422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onward!<br /> <br /> <b>Sekhem</b><br /> <br /> The illustration is great, for that matter. It matches perfectly the one in my head.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would have liked it more if not for the hip firing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:25:29-07:00","id":1204610,"title":"","content":"I don't want to feel like I'm competing with @Jen for your Likes or whatever as we assess the book in front of us; both because treating it like a competition isn't a healthy attitude to have, <i>and</i> because if it <i>were</i> a competition, Jen would be winning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As such, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1202960-a-sfw-thread-where-i-read-arms-of-the-chosen-to-find-the-perfect-sword-boyfriend\">here's a link to Jen's read-through of the same book!</a><br /> <br /> <b>Shipbreaker</b><br /> <br /> This one's got an intriguing story; it sheds a little light on the struggle with the Niobraran, and even reinforces the theme of humanity at the core of every Exalted by having Ianthe put her tribe first not once, but twice.<br /> <br /> I also rather enjoy that this thing's stats factor the naval combat rules in. <br /> <br /> I <i>also</i> like that Shipbreaker is to the water what Marvel Comics' Mjolnir is to the air; the image of a Solar zooming at breakneck speed behind a black jade crossbow is the right mix of cheesy and awesome to make me break out in a huge grin.<br /> <br /> Back to the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I am <i>so</i> glad that cumbrous bolts don't get to be used against human-scale opponents. Whew! <br /> <br /> I might have to borrow that whirlpool's mechanics when I get around to statting my big aquatic baddie.<br /> <br /> <b>Sirrush</b><br /> <br /> Ooh, another artifact flame weapon\u2026 but this one's <i>blue</i> jade. No, but seriously, what might just make for a palette-swap and some shifted numbers in 2e, <i>Sirrush genuinely feels like a different weapon</i>. <b>That's</b> the kind of thing that keeps me gushing about 3e. <br /> <br /> <b>Strife's Crucible</b><br /> <br /> Once again, one of the immediate fun aspects of this artifact is something that jumps out before you even get to the Evocations: with this weapon <i>made by a Sidereal</i>, you can use the fight itself as a means to instruct your opponent! That feels <i>very</i> appropriate!<br /> <br /> Moreover, the &quot;this Evocation awakens at no cost when&quot; for Gleaming Dagger Dissent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know I said it before, about how much these artifacts are intended to guide one towards telling a certain kind of story, but I'll say it again, because it's something I'm really jazzed about! Artifacts like these have <i>really</i> given me reason to think a lot about my characters' Intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-08-2018, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:27:53-07:00","id":1205498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1204610#post1204610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to feel like I'm competing with @Jen for your Likes or whatever as we assess the book in front of us; both because treating it like a competition isn't a healthy attitude to have, <i>and</i> because if it <i>were</i> a competition, Jen would be winning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that, I plan to just review the Artifacts themselves, but somehow it ends up as me making long posts about every paragraph instead...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T02:59:34-07:00","id":1252999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1203422#post1203422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Nightmare Shard</b><br /> <br /> I <i>know</i> this weapon is a boomerang, but it took until Dream-Rending Strike for my mind's eye to stop seeing it as a sword. I'm sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1252739#post1252739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmare Shard began life as a daiklave, but when we were redlining Arms, we realized we had too many damn daiklaves, and not enough non-Melee weapons, so some got tweaked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>knew</i> it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T03:08:21-07:00","id":1253001,"title":"","content":"<b>Sunflash</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThe fluff on Sunflash is fun - back in the days of 2e, I liked the bit in the fluff for the Prayer Piece about how the weapons were designed with the generation of prayers in mind (less so the bit about the micro-shrines to micro-least-gods, but thankfully that's not something that's carried over). I also enjoy the notion of the god being invested enough in the wellbeing of the weapon to see to it that it finds a worthy wielder.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd all that's from before we get to the Evocations!<br /> <br /> Having the weapon have its own anima banner was an interesting direction, and I rather enjoy how that's integrated into its combat utility. Its ability to steal other people's anima banners seems really useful against an uppity Dawn, and the requirement of obtaining the blessing of Kiragaru is an interesting gateway for Incandescent Sunfire Ascendancy.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Talion</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI'll be honest, I've never been a fan of the &quot;mortal Exalts as a Solar to thrash a Solar who underestimated him as a mortal&quot; story that I've seen crop up from time to time on forums when people are arguing about how mortals matter in the Exalted setting, but this seems to avoid all the annoying and condescending bits. Plus, it's a cane for beating up assholes with; I <i>have</i> to approve of that!<br /> <br /> \u200bI like that declaring someone an offender is something of a two-edged sword, as well - sure, you can make sure no one can dissuade you from your quest for stick-hittery, but if you act against it yourself, a Limit Break is all but assured. I particularly enjoy the sort of dogged determination that springs from the wielder of this weapon, represented with the auto-successes to tracking and feats of strength and demolition, the second Willpower track, and the two failure rerolls. Finally, being able to set the offender straight with Rise Up, Penitent! <i>or</i> doom them with Curse of Talion makes for an ultimately versatile weapon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Vainglory</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAn altogether different weapon than Sunflash, despite also being an orichalcum infinite chakram. I rather enjoy how different these weapons can be made to feel. Plus, y'all know me, I'm a sucker for the Solar who takes the crystallized blood of his enemies and sets them as the jewels on his crown. I like the concept of Conceit; my Twilight, Spider, would definitely be tempted by this crown, with his Principle of &quot;Anything that's worth doing, is worth doing in style.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-10-2018, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T04:33:51-07:00","id":1253016,"title":"","content":"<b>Zelator</b><br /> <br /> \u200bRight away I get that good pulpy rush, reading the blurb for this spear. Imagining the torments of Ostra Luka for ten years in that distant hell-world, an enmity for sorcery certainly pervades this weapon. But this is <i>also</i> the weapon of a mounted warrior, and its Evocations make it clear not to forget that. I love how you can use it to bounce a Death Ray back at your attacker, Master Sword-style.<br /> <br /> Plus, horse-hair tassels on weapons are so cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>The Forgotten Blade</b><br /> <br /> ...the what, now?<br /> <br /> \u200bOh, right, yeah. I'm having a hard time remem-<br /> <br /> \u200bAh, just kidding. I have a bit of a history with this one, and I must admit, I approached it with some trepidation this time around. But like so many of these artifacts, I found myself positively giddy before I even got to its list of Evocations. The mechanics for memory-excising gambits is so much more elegant than my memories of the old weapon.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, this weapon kinda terrifies me now. It's a good thing I wasn't gonna sleep anytime soon, because I think I'd have nightmares about losing my memories if I did.<br /> <br /> <b>Gorgon</b><br /> <br /> Meep.<br /> <br /> This artifact is a pretty neat example of how other splats can gain Resonance with an otherwise-incompatible material by dint of other affinities. It's also very visceral-feeling, with its blood-drinking, its petrification abilities, and the huge evil eye on the blade. The Wakefulness mechanic seems pretty solid; thank goodness it's possible to sing it to sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-10-2018, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T04:53:31-07:00","id":1253019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1253016#post1253016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good thing I wasn't gonna sleep anytime soon, because I think I'd have nightmares about losing my memories to this thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Would</i> have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T08:32:19-07:00","id":1253594,"title":"","content":"<b>Soulfarer</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThis Stormbringer-esque battle-axe doesn't mess around; its writeup evokes undead monstrosities, an empire of necromancers, and its first bearer's slide into depravity. I can't help but wonder how the Great Curse might have manifested with Yasha Vol, and if maybe her circle-mates were too quick to place all of the blame on this admittedly-bloodthirsty weapon.<br /> <br /> That said, its intended playstyle is pretty apparent, given the special unlocking mechanic for Pain-Eating Empowerment. Though it amuses me that its current bearer is pledging her victories to the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> <b>Stormcaller</b><br /> <br /> \u200bWe've seen this before, but I'm still impressed with this. It's <i>very</i> potent, all too appropriate for a five-dot artifact. From Double 7s on a Withering attack roll, all the way to replicating Rain of Doom, this artifact <i>needs</i> a one-ton puzzle box to contain it.<br /> <br /> <b>Overview</b><br /> <br /> \u200bWe've seen some powerful artifacts in this chapter. This collection of storied god-weapons brings a surge of vitality and imagination. The writing makes my skin tingle; these blades and bows and hammers and staves <i>feel</i> powerful, in a way that previous treatments often didn't. From being able to outfit yourself in the finest silks, to wrapping a band around someone's heart to turn their hate to love, to cursing a region with mist, to leaving someone an amnesiac at a single sword-stroke, the presence of even one of these potent tools can be a genuine game-changer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1158815-arms-of-the-chosen?p=1160536#post1160536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a notion about five-dot Artifact weapons in which the thing in common between them isn't so much a power that corrupts, as a power that is great enough to require being handled with care.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen thinking about their basic comparisons measured against the lower levels, the term that came to my mind is that five-dots are <b>brimming</b> with power. That can come in forms such as the corebook, where they accumulate and unleash energy just from being used in combat, or some of our new ones with things like an entry-level power that is quite strong, up to things like Stormcaller where just pulling the thing out causes a growing manifestation; all depending on the Artifact's temperament. You're holding a lightning bolt, something that twists around and vibrates in your hand, and while it's not necessarily dangerous to you, you've got to keep a tight grasp to actually direct it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's how I would characterize the cascade of their Evocations; three-dots' flow into you, adding some colour to the edges of your actions, and four-dots' try to shape you, creating a channel for you to act within, while five-dots have their own thing going on and your part is to focus and refine that, bending the manifestations of its power to your own will and needs, whether that be applying that in ways that are somewhat novel, or at least pointing it in the direction you want before taking the latch off the door. Depending on its nature, that might sometimes make you open to some kind of influence, but it's mostly a subject of keeping a handle on this power as you use it (since, in most cases, the Artifact can hardly use itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>You said it, dude. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-16-2018, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T11:45:08-07:00","id":1253656,"title":"","content":"Yay, you're back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T10:50:56-07:00","id":1254560,"title":"","content":"Armor's always kind of in a weird head-space with me. Weapons are super-versatile, to serve a range of lethal and nonlethal purposes, and as such, there's a huge amount of room for Evocations to vary there; armor, on the other hand, is pretty much always designed first and foremost to serve as protection for the wearer, and the degree to which a chain shirt and a buff jacket <i>are</i> different largely falls below the level of system resolution... so I'd expect its range of Evocations to be a bit narrower.<br /> <br /> <b>Baldaquin</b><br /> <br /> Baldaquin's pretty solid for a traveling negotiator-type, often by way of improving on already-potent Solar Charms; I'm glad to see the armor being passed down in its story.<br /> <br /> <b>Heartsbalm</b><br /> <br /> Always pleasant to see another positive gay couple in the setting. You hardly need Indomitable Guardian Ardor's special unlocking method to incentivize a story of you and your beloved triumphing against all odds; practically its entire suite of Evocations builds toward that. One little thing that sticks out, though: I'm a little confused as to how Laughing Sky managed to attune the armor when his beloved, Oak Ring Prince, was dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Kaijin</b><br /> <br /> I like the notion of a Sidereal crafter drawing spiritual power out of something to imbue their artifact with it. The writer of this artifact did a pretty solid job on grasping that certain intangible feel, even if it doesn't quite jibe with how &quot;dematerialized&quot; sits in my brain.<br /> <br /> <b>Midnight Thorn</b><br /> <br /> Sometimes I wonder about hearthstone slots on artifacts. Some of the writeups don't mention where the hearthstones go at all, but other times it's very exact about it. Love to see an artifact that's a product of the Second Age. And being able to throw a flower that turns into a wall of briars for you to duck behind, that's pretty awesome. I imagine that instead of the Evocations enhancing Solar Stealth and such, a DB wearer might expand in the &quot;growing thorny defenses&quot; direction.<br /> <br /> <b>Five Edicts Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <i>Fuck</i> yeah. Whispering black armor with Spikes of Villainy, forged from the Old Laws and the souls of long-extinct pre-humans, and buried for millennia? That's <b>metal as hell</b>, and I love it. I am not using figurative language when I say that I got a chill down my spine when I read the Evocation <i>On Your Knees</i>.<br /> <br /> Whoever wrote this artifact, I implore you: if you ever meet me IRL, <i>tell me you wrote it</i>. I'll buy you dinner. Probably McDonald's or something, given my current financial situation.<br /> <br /> <b>The Quincunx</b><br /> <br /> I didn't expect to see a reference to Devon in this edition; at least, not until the sorcery book, but this is <i>very</i> intriguing. The description is very vivid - I feel certain that the image in my head is a near-match for the one in the writer's.<br /> <br /> It's past my bedtime, so I'm in no state of mind to be doing math, but this looks like a pretty potent battery for sorcery. I'm glad to see a <i>light</i> armor be one of the higher-rated ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-15-2018, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T11:28:07-07:00","id":1254568,"title":"","content":"My friend's evil warlord uses Five Edicts Dominion, it's very fitting.<br /> <br /> I think you'll really enjoy Sozen, the level 5 orichalcum plate. It's a lot of fun, and quite original. But maybe, of the artefact armours, the one that's most character significant.<br /> <br /> The blue jade armour has a great capstone, and a fun piece of art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T18:47:31-07:00","id":1254667,"title":"","content":"I like to think of armour as also being able to function as a kind of uniform, signifying a personal role or function and providing a slightly wider ranger of enhancements through that lens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1254568#post1254568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you'll really enjoy Sozen, the level 5 orichalcum plate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still only level 4, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T21:41:34-07:00","id":1254688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1254667#post1254667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think of armour as also being able to function as a kind of uniform, signifying a personal role or function and providing a slightly wider ranger of enhancements through that lens.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong; I <i>am</i> glad that there's so many not-strictly-defensive Evocations available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T02:58:59-07:00","id":1254727,"title":"","content":"Yeah, considering that the most readily available artifact materials are the 5MM, which are all metals or rocks, it makes sense that the easiest way to make artifact clothing is for it to be armour. So if you just want a wearable effect, you stick it on a chain shirt or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T06:05:09-07:00","id":1254752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1254727#post1254727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, considering that the most readily available artifact materials are the 5MM, which are all metals or rocks, it makes sense that the easiest way to make artifact clothing is for it to be armour. So if you just want a wearable effect, you stick it on a chain shirt or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Cloth of jade&quot; is a thing in Creation; if even jade-alloy is ductile enough to turn into wires that can be woven together with fibers or even without fibers to make cloth...<br /> <br /> Well, a pure cloth-of-jade garment is likely protective enough to count as light armor. Fiber-and-alloy cloth might count as less than light armor, being merely magical clothing, but when the fibers are made some indestructible fire-rat fur or else enchanted to be properly indestructible for an artifact...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 09-16-2018, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T06:14:34-07:00","id":1254754,"title":"","content":"I never said they <i>couldn't</i> make artifact clothing. I said artifact armour was <i>easier. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T06:20:10-07:00","id":1254755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1254754#post1254754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said they <i>couldn't</i> make artifact clothing. I said artifact armour was <i>easier. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Clothing is easier to make than armor, especially chain-mail or plate armor.<br /> <br /> It would also require smaller (cheaper) amounts of magical metal.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how it should be more difficult for a craftsman, though I concede it's generally more difficult for the writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T07:12:45-07:00","id":1254763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1254755#post1254755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clothing is easier to make than armor, especially chain-mail or plate armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless Cloth of Jade is just insanely difficult and time consuming to make compared to hammering rings and metal sheets into forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T08:01:35-07:00","id":1254770,"title":"","content":"There may also not be enough jade to channel the magic.<br /> <br /> Frankly though, I don't see any inherent problem with magic clothes. Magic gloves, belts, cloaks, etc. And in fact, there is a magic cloak and magic shoes in Arms. There's just less of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T08:08:33-07:00","id":1254771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1254763#post1254763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless Cloth of Jade is just insanely difficult and time consuming to make compared to hammering rings and metal sheets into forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you get a spool of magical wire from someone else, that makes it a lot easier.<br /> <br /> How difficult it is to stretch the alloys into wire is a mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T08:32:23-07:00","id":1254776,"title":"","content":"All I was saying was that there is a logical basis for artifact armour that has utility effects with nothing to do with protecting the wearer to be fairly common, not that alternatives were impossible. <br /> <br /> Even in the first age the exalted were fairly military and ran around adventuring, so armour was useful to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T10:22:36-07:00","id":1254785,"title":"","content":"Y'all remember that artifact armour includes things like buff jackets or leather jerkins with maybe a bit of metal in them, if that, right? <br /> <br /> I mean, magical armour that is full plate is already generally going to be highly ornate, so I don't think that it's much of a stretch to assume that there are occasionally going to be Artifact buff jackets that would be hard to distinguish from something like court uniform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T12:14:37-07:00","id":1254815,"title":"","content":"Unity is actually a set of (stylish) black clothes, which the user can transform into, IIRC, mail, a tight-fitting complete set of mail, or an all-encompassing suit of heavy armour. In its base form (which still gives you the stats of medium artefact armour) it doesn't look like armour at all (though it does give -1 mobility...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T20:24:04-07:00","id":1254908,"title":"","content":"<b>Sozen, the Cataphract of Keys</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThis here is pretty damn cool. The writing is evocative, the visuals are cool, and its story is definitely one of those things that really belongs in the Exalted setting - I can easily imagine a Second or even Third Circle demon that just naturally appears in the shape of an apparently-empty suit of armor.<br /> <br /> As I read its capstone, I can't help but imagine a hypothetical Solar who has wandered Creation learning the ways of heart-ripping. He's mastered Black Claw Style and learned the Brawl Charms, and then he comes across this armor...<br /> <br /> <b>Mela's Coil</b><br /> <br /> \u200bLovely illustration, more fun incentives stuff, though I'll take its backstory with Devourer of Graves as a cautionary tale - sometimes, people don't give a shit about what you think.<br /> <br /> When I first read this one's writeup, I genuinely said, &quot;If this doesn't have letting you turn into a dragon as its capstone, I'm gonna write it in there.&quot; Glad to see we're on the same page! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Speaking of being on the same page...<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Unity</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI'll admit, I'm less fond of Artifacts that no one has any business knowing about - this one was made by one person, by herself in an empty palace, who then killed thousands of Fair Folk by herself before dying. Don't get me wrong, this is a fun artifact, but it wasn't forgotten by time - it was never <i>learned</i> by time. But that's a relatively minor quibble, Unity is pretty badass.<br /> <br /> Just being able to do the mien stuff without so much as learning a single Evocation is pretty potent; this suit's inclusion in the five-dot category seems pretty concrete.<br /> <br /> <b>Overview</b><br /> <br /> \u200bArmor's always been kind of important to survival in the Exalted setting; the Chosen, after all, are beings of flesh. They are not invulnerable, but putting a few bits of jadesteel between the assassin's knives and your internal organs goes a long way.<br /> <br /> And as demonstrated here, the hauberks made by the Chosen have so much more potential than I might have initially thought; in fact, I feel bad for the player who buys artifact armor for the soak/hardness, and then never spends XP on Evocations for it. Though at least if they read through these, they'll have an idea of what they're missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-16-2018, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T03:00:52-07:00","id":1254959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1254908#post1254908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can easily imagine a Second or even Third Circle demon that just naturally appears in the shape of an apparently-empty suit of armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but I feel as though the concept of the thing is more fun if the magic of it means that other demons don't recognise that Sozen is a suit of armour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'll admit, I'm less fond of Artifacts that no one has any business knowing about - this one was made by one person, by herself in an empty palace, who then killed thousands of Fair Folk by herself before dying. Don't get me wrong, this is a fun artifact, but it wasn't forgotten by time - it was never <i>learned</i> by time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, Nara-O will know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T03:22:29-07:00","id":1254962,"title":"","content":"I consider the backstories more suggestions anyway. If a PC wants one you might need to tweak a few details to get it to them for chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T07:51:58-07:00","id":1255001,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I used the backstory of God-Speed Vanguard pretty straight, but I think if you want to alter them its fine. Or you could start with the same beginning (it's not really the same artefact otherwise) but add something about someone finding them.<br /> I do see Alucard's point though.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Isator, you were right about Sozen's rating. For some reason, my pdf gives the ratings for every artefact on the bookmarks tab except Sozen, and since it was just before two level 5 artefacts, I assumed it was level 5 as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T08:26:45-07:00","id":1255493,"title":"","content":"So, bad news. I'd written up some for the next chapter on my laptop, when the cat pushed it off onto the floor, damaging the charger. I won't be able to get a new charger just yet, either. I'm posting from my phone, but reading PDFs on it is a pain-and-a-half.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T16:44:05-08:00","id":1279811,"title":"","content":"Hey, y'all, finally got my replacement charger.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Natural Magics</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI love the little stuff like this. Things that are too strange and mystical to sit on the shelf in a marketplace, but not quite potent or lasting enough to necessitate Artifact dots. We've got a lot of classics here, but I don't recognize Dawnflower; is it new? Either way, it's pretty neat. I've already pestered my ST to retroactively assume my Eclipse owns a dreamstone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Audient Brush</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAnother old classic, wasn't expecting my socks to be knocked off by it. To be fair, most of its thunder was probably stolen earlier by Sun's Brush. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Clockwork Bird/Bird of Vanileth</b><br /> <br /> Thanks for the clarification on First Age artifice. I've never been too big on spending dots on Familiar or anything else that amounts to a small animal; daiklaves and the like might be able to be stolen, but at least they're relatively hard to destroy. But I realize this is just my stupid, scarred-by-2e brain getting in the way of a pretty neat artifact. Plus, this one's at least hardier than your standard small bird. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Lorestone</b><br /> <br /> \u200bFairly basic, but not in a bad way. I love the inclusion of First Age cuisine in the list of subjects.<br /> <br /> <b>Lotus-Blossom Cup</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAnother classic. Its interaction with the disease and poison rules are a reminder of how pleasantly simple the rules for those are now, and thus I love it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Solar Seal/Auspicious Secret Seal</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI rather enjoy the elemental variations that occur by making these out of blue, black, or red jade, and brings to mind the thought of what might happen with other materials. Perhaps a green jade one would cause the missive to blossom into a flower? I wonder what a starmetal one might do, for that matter...<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Stoneheart Coffer</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI actually like that it protects against jostling and the elements, but not against time itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Ultimately Useful Tube</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAgain, fairly basic, but not bad. I'm curious as to what's so special about the Liar's Tree; is this a reference to something I've missed?<br /> <br /> <b>Winterbreath Jar</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI'm enjoying the added clause about plugging in an Air-aspected hearthstone.<br /> <br /> <b>Arete</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThe first new artifact of the chapter, I gotta say, the inclusion of a backstory makes this artifact so much more vivid. Its Evocations really resonate with the story, too.<br /> <br /> <b>Carnelian Phoenix</b><br /> <br /> \u200bOnce again, y'all have an artifact that's cool before we even get to the Evocations. I'll have to look at the Ride rules again, but this seems pretty neat for such a character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T16:56:47-08:00","id":1279816,"title":"","content":"Starmetal Seal - ...note? What note? The envelope was empty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T03:12:52-08:00","id":1280456,"title":"","content":"<b>Dragon Tear Tiara</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAn old classic, this seems handy for an Occult character; I might end up having to dig one up for Spider. I'll have to keep an eye on future publications to see how it interacts with Sidereal, Lunar, et cetera., spirit detection.<br /> <br /> <b>The Golden Hounds</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI like the story of this one. Is the Sand mentioned the same one from <i>Caste Book: Eclipse</i>? The Celerity mechanic looks like fun, too. I especially enjoy that the ecstatic speed granted by the Golden Hounds is limited in its capacity to be used for offense; sure, you can use it to evade attacks as you Rush an enemy, but the second you actually hit him, your bonus resets to 0 as if you'd stopped moving altogether. It reinforces their nature as a runner's boots, not a fighter's.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I also enjoy the shout-out to Ruvia.)<br /> <br /> <b>Illusion-Shattering Mirror</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThe power of coincidence is strong; I happened to also be hearing the introduction for the audiobook of Neil Gaiman's <i>Smoke and Mirrors</i> at the same time as I was reading this one. I rather enjoy how one can use this mirror to not only break an enemy's disguise - you can use it to help a someone destroy a false belief they hold. This might be really handy to have for when a Solar goes too far with Memory-Reweaving Discipline. Still, <i>they</i> have to be the one to discard it; the lie might be too comfortable for them to cease hiding behind it.<br /> <br /> <b>Jade Steed</b><br /> <br /> (double-checks horse stats)<br /> <br /> \u200bOkay, yeah, this is cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Resplendent Satchel of Healing</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI didn't like the old version of the Satchel; Seamstress of Dissolution's player wanted one in my Okeanos game, and so I went combing through the Second Edition books to uncover it. When I finally found it, I asked her, &quot;Why? All it does is render the Medicine Charms on your sheet obsolete!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThis one feels more like it complements a healer character, rather than replacing her.<br /> <br /> <b>Second-Shadow Drum</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAhh, a human-skin drum; <i>this</i> feels pretty damn pulpy. It also seems like the guy who has this also has the envy of every necromancer on the block.<br /> <br /> <b>Brass Legionnaire</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThese guys seem like top-notch combatants, pulling slightly ahead of even a Dawn's Tiger-Warriors. I also appreciate the sidebar about making batches of these guys; even a dedicated Twilight isn't going to be able to just litter the setting with these things.<br /> <br /> <b>Collar of Dutiful Submission</b><br /> <br /> \u200bFor all your Monkey King-restraining needs. It wouldn't have occurred to me to make the Stamina + Resistance roll require a flurry to do anything else, but that seems like a pretty solid way to represent struggling against its tightening without making the character completely helpless. I like it!<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Shadow-Casting Jewel</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThis one's pretty niche, given its short-range limitation and once-per-month usability, but still makes for a <i>very</i> nasty surprise. I recently reread Niven's &quot;Not Long Before the End,&quot; and this feels like one of the kinds of things the Warlock would squirrel away for a confrontation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T03:01:11-08:00","id":1280658,"title":"","content":"<b>Sorcery-Capturing Cord</b><br /> <br /> \u200bAnother old classic. This one is a tad dangerous, as it requires you to stand in the path of a sorcerer while he's shaping a spell, and hope that your fingers are quicker with knots than his mind is with channeling mystic energies. On the upside, if you pull it off, you can save that Death Ray for a rainy day. The idea that you might come across one with a spell already tied up in it is pretty intriguing, especially paired with the chance of <i>knot </i>knowing what it is.<br /> <br /> \u200bRobin: &quot;There's a spell already trapped in this cord.&quot;<br /> Knight Raiton: &quot;What is it?&quot;<br /> \u200bRobin: &quot;I don't know, but it's Solar circle.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Wings of the Raptor</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI like the mythic origin of these wings, and that you've actually gotta have room to fly around with the 20-foot wingspan that'd be required to give a human enough lift to fly. The old wings of the raptor from previous editions felt rather easy to pass up, and wasn't helped by how interchangeable even wings of different materials were.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it's a good move, giving the first Evocation a discount for having the right Charms. Its capstone is super good; I hope folks aren't discouraged by the &quot;keep it attuned for a full story&quot; requirement of its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <b>The Golden Viper</b><br /> <br /> A talking venomous snake that offers knowledge that leaves you no longer innocent, seemingly working toward its own mysterious agenda. Plus he turns his victims into solid gold. This is definitely a five-dot artifact, all right. I also like the way in which it demonstrates the difference between its ilk, and automatons that <i>aren't</i> works of First Age Artifice.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>The Veil That Holds Back Time</b><br /> <br /> \u200bKickass name, vivid description. I'm not a huge fan of easily-destroyed artifacts (as stated above and elsewhere), but considering that this one wasn't made with any of the magical materials, I can dig it. I'm not entirely convinced that its utility necessitates five dots, but it's definitely cool.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Siege Weapons</b><br /> <br /> \u200bOne game session from my Okeanos game had some of the PCs fighting on another ship while Seamstress stayed behind with the mortal crew; unbeknownst to them, a shark-god child of Siakal had come aboard the circle's ship intent on slaughtering the crew in their absence. Seamstress surprised it by tackling the thing and locking her arms around its throat. The rest of the crew, heartened by her brave antics, beset the thing with knives and belaying pins, and one of them unloaded a couple of ballista bolts into it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe shark-god very wisely decided to dematerialize after that, but Seamstress maintained her death-grip even across the chasm of the material, and strangled it to death.<br /> <br /> \u200bAt the time, these rules hadn't been published, so I just kinda winged it. But I'm glad to see that my ST instincts weren't <i>too</i> far from the mark. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Ballista</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI'm a little surprised that you can throw an unblockable lightning bolt and have it not be a decisive attack. This bad boy's definitely something to tread lightly with, both because of its capacity for friendly fire, and because deciding to deploy a Stormblast Barrage means it'll require maintenance after.*<br /> <br /> <b>Implosion Bow</b><br /> <br /> \u200bIt feels a bit redundant to say that it's unblockable <i>and</i> automatically hits battle groups, but then again, maybe I just don't pay enough attention to Evasion. Combining the withering effect on top of the decisive implosion, plus destroying structures and objects, <i>plus</i> devastating battle groups, <i>plus</i> leaving behind difficult terrain, <b><i>definitely</i></b> says Artifact 5 to me.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b><i>Horizon Endeavor</i></b><br /> <br /> *jaw drops*<br /> <br /> \u200bI was unprepared for how badass an artifact warship would be. Beware the Sail Supernal Solar who gets Blood and Salt Bondage and sets his sights on <i>Horizon Endeavor</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Chariot of Aerial Conquest</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI'm glad this thing doesn't have any integrated weapons - I don't know if I would've been able to handle it.<br /> <br /> I like this one, as I'm not particularly fond of airships that look <i>exactly</i> like sailing ships. Having it be a giant five-sided howdah (<i>sans</i> elephant) made of gold makes for a pretty unique airship.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b*At first I misread these bits, thinking it would require maintenance after every shot, limiting it to a once-per-combat affair, but a subsequent rereading showed me that it doesn't actually require the maintenance until after the scene is over. That's <i>much</i> better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-14-2019, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T03:33:50-08:00","id":1280661,"title":"","content":"The Veil makes a good combo with the Stoneheart Coffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T03:54:04-08:00","id":1280663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1280661#post1280661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Veil makes a good combo with the Stoneheart Coffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had a First Age Dragonblooded planned who had survived by being mummfied in the Veil and stored in a Stoneheart Coffin","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T16:21:30-08:00","id":1282921,"title":"","content":"<b>Warstriders</b><br /> \u200bNow we finally get to the long-anticipated chapter on the walking war-engines of the First Age. I've been excited about these since I first heard about them. The execution's always felt a bit off in previous editions; there were few foes a Solar could face where they'd genuinely be better off fighting from a thirty-foot-high relic-armor of legend, and that's just disappointing.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut this edition seems to have nailed it. The free Devastate action really puts the <b>war</b> in warstrider, and its ability to ignore the benefits of Legendary Size (while enjoying those benefits itself against smaller-scale opponents!) makes it very formidable even before we get to Evocations.<br /> <br /> Already my breath is taken away by the artwork and fiction. Even though the Solar seriously threatens the life of the Dragon-Blooded pilot, this pyroclastic metal titan feels appropriately powerful and massive.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, let's get to the named ones, shall we?<br /> <br /> <b>All-Conquering Colossus</b><br /> \u200bGreat name, great story. For those of you who can't read along, this orichalcum titan was created by a Twilight looking to reunite with and protect her circle's Dawn, who had sworn an oath to defeat all of Creation's enemies. Encased as she was in the warstrider, the Dawn didn't recognize the Twilight at first, but after a few rounds of combat, she realized who she was fighting. They were wed soon after.<br /> <br /> Once again, even before we get to its Evocations, we see that this thing is meant to shrug off lesser attacks and slay giant horrors. Sure enough, its first two Evocations showcase this. Rita Repulsa-alikes, beware: this mecha won't just <i>defeat</i> your sorcerously-enlarged behemoths - it'll fling them back at your moon-palace with enough force to topple its towers.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation</b><br /> \u200bWe receive yet another hint about the enigmatic Scorpion Empire in this thing's blurb. This sun-metal weapons platform is <i>bristling</i> with deadly weaponry, made to stand against otherworldly enemies from the Wyld and stranger places. \u200bAnyone who's ever felt like warstriders are a little too punch-focused for their Archery character: this is the warstrider for you. Concealed within it are reserves of firedust, massive crossbow bolts, flechettes, lightning ballistae, and of course its Godsigh of Noonday Triumph.<br /> <br /> <b>Crusading Spear of the Depths</b><br /> \u200bOur first non-orichalcum one, this black jade warstrider was created by a familiar Sidereal to do battle against the Niobrarans. The warstrider's inaugural pilot tragically lost her life in the conflict, but brought down the armies of the Spoken with her via Crusading Spear's devastating Ocean-Twisting Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd like to note that while this metal giant <i>is</i> specialized for underwater combat, many of its Evocations have at least some application in combat on land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-26-2019, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T16:25:20-08:00","id":1283140,"title":"","content":"<b>Emerald Chevalier</b><br /> This is the unparalleled choice for the combatant who wants to play at mounted combat but doesn't want to breed a warstrider-sized horse. Emerald Chevalier is a four-legged green jade warstrider in the shape of a woman riding a horse. Her first wearer tragically neglected to perform maintenance on Emerald Chevalier, and then was killed by nomads while trying to unstrap herself from it. Damaged beyond the Shogunate's ability to repair it, Emerald Chevalier was enshrined in some ruin or another.<br /> <br /> \u200bI very much enjoy this potent warstrider; its Evocations are those of a swift, tireless charger, impaling foes on her lance or trampling them underhoof, culminating in an ultimate technique in which the lance impact sends out a massive shockwave.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Godspeed Vanguard</b><br /> \u200bThis is a lightly-armored scout of a warstrider, capable of stealth and various optical tricks, drawing on orichalcum's themes of light <i>and</i> shadow equally. I find it worth mentioning how its blurb details its use in a conflict between Solars battling for dominance over Creation in a period apparently called the Sunstrife Wars.<br /> <br /> \u200b(This is actually intriguing; let's hope it's not explored and demystified in a disappointing way, like the Clone Wars.)<br /> <br /> \u200bOh, also it can flash brightly enough to burn out mortal eyes, and that's not even the capstone.<br /> <br /> \u200b*rechecks Living Wind Approach*<br /> <br /> \u200bYep, okay, that's more powerful. This one deserves its five Artifact dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T20:12:42-08:00","id":1283178,"title":"","content":"Emerald Chevalier also comes with a bow and Evocations that assist with Aiming, so it can shoot at targets as it charges into melee range with them, and as it retreats.<br /> <br /> Among the non-flying warstriders of the book, it is the supreme hit-and-run champion, though it obviously gets into trouble if it cannot extricate itself from close range with opponents like All-Conquering Colossus, and Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation can really put on the hurt from a distance before Emerald Chevalier can get close enough to overwhelm its meager close range power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T05:57:43-08:00","id":1283241,"title":"","content":"Indeed it does; yesterday was a bit stressful for me, and I in fact overlooked some details.<br /> <br /> I saved the N/A's for last, let's take a look.<br /> <br /> <u>\u200b<i><b>Ascendant Nova Phoenix</b></i></u><br /> <br /> Designed to be the supreme flying warstrider (and indeed, the only one published in this book capable of flight), this orichalcum war machine was created by a team of three Exalts who used Wyld-based time-dilation to finish their project in secret. This thing is glorious, with a blue jade wings and individually crafted feathers of orichalcum. The pilot operates from a sphere of adamant that can display what the warstrider sees to the pilot (and the rest of his circle, as there's room for them in the fuselage!); in idle time, it plays through visions of some of its more legendary deeds.<br /> <br /> \u200bNaturally, creating something this awesome led to the makers turning on each other; we're not told which one ended up with this amazing device and went on to shape the Age.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis thing can kick all kinds of ass; Ascendant Nova Phoenix can fly at (Essence x500) miles per hour, and can perform many sorts of aerial maneuvers above and beyond what's allowed with humble wings, without even a single purchased Evocation. Once you start buying those, you're capable of creating burning landscapes, damaging whirlwinds, or pillars of fire, or showers of holy burning feathers, or sonic booms; often just as a <i>by-product</i> of making an attack. Its Evocations intersect at many points with the Solar Charmset, enhancing the already-pretty-amazing Heavenly Guardian Defense, Eye of the Unconquered Sun, and Eagle Wing Style. Its pinnacle Evocation permits you to fly fast enough to cross Creation itself inside of an hour.<br /> <br /> Ascendant Nova Phoenix very much lives up to its name and its hype. It stands at twice the height of other warstriders. If you knew you were going to duel Ligier in an hour, <i>this</i> would be the suit you'd put on. It absolutely deserves its N/A rating, as its battlefield-scarring glory transcends the notion of game balance and glows fiercely enough to dim the rest of Creation by comparison.<br /> <br /> And that's not even the last one in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-28-2019, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T06:21:43-08:00","id":1283243,"title":"","content":"Oh, the next one is going to be a fun one. Looking forward to your reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T06:41:19-08:00","id":1283245,"title":"","content":"<b><i><u>Karvara the Walking Devil-Tower</u></i></b><br /> <br /> \u200bThere was once a monster that lay dormant in Zen-Mu. It was turned loose by Feng Huang Morningstar, a Solar traitor, and where the monster was, Creation <i>was not</i>. A hundred Exalted working together subdued Karvara, pinned the horrific creature down, but even then they <i>could not kill it</i>. A Lunar and Solar worked on it from within and without, working molten moonsilver over the beast to imprison its apocalyptic body inside a massive warstrider. The warstrider's fuselage is a hollowed-out portion of the beast's spine, and its controls hook directly into Karvara's nervous system; the pilot and the beast may even communicate with each other through this link.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe beast is not content to meekly serve, either; it quietly seeks to influence and corrupt the pilot, for in the midst of Limit Break, Karvara may assert control over the moonsilver limbs of the warstrider. Even that is not enough - it wants to be <i>free</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bAfter the Usurpation, Karvara was entombed with its pilot, and sealed behind the sinews of dragons and the silk of Pattern Spiders, with just a touch of the Silent Wind of Malfeas. Naturally, the agent Heaven sent to check on it after the Jade Prison was broken has gone missing.<br /> <br /> \u200bHoo boy. This moonsilver monstrosity is a vicious and terrifying bastard. It won't even accept you as a pilot if you're not cursed enough for it to corrupt you. Its Evocations are monstrous and aptly-named; the first, &quot;Eat the Heart of God,&quot; slides back the armored plate over the warstrider's mouth to reveal a toothy maw that can swallow whole fallen foes of less than Legendary Size. Karvara can permanently destroy spirits in this fashion, and eaten creatures yield tasty, tasty Initiative. Its Evocations often reward the pilot who gains Limit at the helm of Karvara, and reap grisly trophies from its slain foes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Torn From This World&quot; is genuinely scary, even months after having read it, this Evocation may keep me from sleeping; you gain it for free when Karvara devours someone you have a Major or Defining Tie towards, at which point eaten foes <i>are erased from history</i>. Even the pilot won't remember someone the warstrider consumes, absent Charms like Invincible Solar Aegis.<br /> <br /> \u200bIts ultimate technique, &quot;Voice of the Apocalypse,&quot; lets Karvara speak a word from the tongue of Zen-Mu, unmaking Creation in an arc that extends out to extreme range, and replacing it with something... <i>else</i>. Enemies caught in the wake of it are Torn From This World.<br /> <br /> \u200bWow. I've got the shivers. This thing needs to be imprisoned forever. I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-29-2019, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T09:46:10-08:00","id":1283292,"title":"","content":"<b>Summary</b><br /> <br /> \u200b<i>Arms of the Chosen</i> is a thoroughly remarkable book, filled with all manner of artifacts for player characters to discover the history of, seek out, or wield in battle. The blades, bows, armors, and amulets contained inside are game-changers, and serve as a shining triumph of the Evocations system. The devs have written artifacts that make me feel like a kid fogging up the glass window of a display with his breath, simultaneously wanting the things displayed within with unmitigated greed, and not feeling worthy of them. Moreover, it's inspired me to come up with artifacts of my own, from Ravenous Shade Prison to Centimane to the Regalia of the Raiton. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1120_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1120\" data-vbnamecard=\"1120\">Eric Minton</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a> should be proud of their work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-28-2019, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T23:33:17-08:00","id":1283457,"title":"","content":"And just in case you ever think Karvara isn\u2019t N/A enough, don\u2019t forget the part where you can <i>buy the Charms of spirits it eats as Evocations</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T06:11:43-08:00","id":1283493,"title":"","content":"You think you'll carry on with the artifacts we get in the fatsplat books? The DB ones are rad and I'm sure Lunars will carry on the tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T06:22:00-08:00","id":1283495,"title":"","content":"They're apparently gonna mostly be weapons.<br /> Maybe a bit of armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T08:17:37-08:00","id":1283510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1283493#post1283493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think you'll carry on with the artifacts we get in the fatsplat books? The DB ones are rad and I'm sure Lunars will carry on the tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I'd love to hear your take on future artifacts, Alucard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T08:23:05-08:00","id":1283512,"title":"","content":"I'd be happy to look over the artifacts from the Dragon-Blooded, and Heirs once it comes out. Having some financial difficulties at present, though, so I don't know how quickly I'll be able to jump into Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T03:55:39-08:00","id":1283678,"title":"","content":"We probably won't get concrete info on lunar artifacts until May~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T04:08:12-08:00","id":1283679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1283678#post1283678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We probably won't get concrete info on lunar artifacts until May~</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough* March.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T06:33:22-08:00","id":1283703,"title":"","content":"On artifacts? Doubt it. Usually the first month or two splits between setting and rules bits. Artifacts are very low priority in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T06:38:48-08:00","id":1283704,"title":"","content":"Yes, but with DBs it took 4 weeks for them to release all the parts. Artefacts were at the end, but it's still 4 weeks.<br /> If the Kickstarter is in 2 weeks, then it should be finished in 6 or 7 weeks, so March.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T06:42:42-08:00","id":1283706,"title":"","content":"Kickstarters only run for a month. We'll have the whole book by the end of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T06:48:31-08:00","id":1283707,"title":"","content":"Nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T04:30:18-07:00","id":1303285,"title":"","content":"Okay, folks, looks like my Exalted session for today was canceled, so I might as well review some Dragon-Blooded artifacts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Calumny</b><br /> <br /> \u200bFirst off, <i>wonderful</i> name. The nod to Dragon-Blooded Larceny is also very nice. It feels very appropriate for an artifact based around the power of secrets to be able to conceal itself effectively, and I like how it grades the power of secrets off the sort of task it would take to reveal it.<br /> <br /> \u200bRustling Grapevine Whispers is a good start, with a fun condition to unlock it; to learn the secrets of others, you must feed the staff a secret of your own. Of course, it occurs to me that absent a means of condensing down the time requirement (which <i>is</i> doable with Dragon-Blooded Charms), it might be impractical to discern a secret through a Profile Character action during combat.<br /> <br /> Salon-Spider Entrapment lets you entangle a foe in their secrets, allowing further entangling if the secret is known to the wielder; paired with the ability of Swallowtail's Grace to unleash a counterattack or even Initiative-draining influence attempt against a foe, the wielder might genuinely Crash an opponent swinging a sledgehammer at her by telling him that she knows how his firstborn <i>really</i> died.<br /> <br /> A wielder who really wants to twist the knife can even use Ripened Bitter Fruit to turn their secrets into actual venom.<br /> <br /> \u200bAll in all, a fun artifact, definitely one that proves to be powerful in the hands of the socialite with a trickster bent to their playstyle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T05:58:30-07:00","id":1303304,"title":"","content":"It also works as a Wood Dragon Style weapon. Exactly half of the Heirlooms are clearly intended to serve as Immaculate Style weapons, though perhaps only one is &quot;properly pious&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T08:01:53-07:00","id":1303530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1196730-alucard-gets-his-grubby-hands-on-aotc?p=1303304#post1303304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also works as a Wood Dragon Style weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, right, forgot the change to Wood Dragon Style.<br /> <br /> <b>Daring Venture</b><br /> <br /> Our second green jade weapon of the book, we start off with some nice characterization for V'neef, providing some details about her adventurous spirit and capacity for compassion. The description of the bow is rather vivid, and I enjoy how the scenery etched into it changes as its wielder travels. Plus, y'know, magic bond to a giant wolf, how cool is that?<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd yes, technically this one is also in-style for Wood Dragon.<br /> <br /> \u200bIts first Evocation awakens for free to a Dragon-Blooded scion of House V'neef, and grants bonuses on Medicine rolls and rolls to influence wild beasts; a Resonant user can also apply a bonus to a beast's Defense, Resolve, or Guile, allowing for some very potent Familiar-boosting.<br /> <br /> \u200bNext up is Seeker's Heart Intuition, which points the wielder in the direction of some as-yet-unvisited location. Simple, fun, and a handy tool for Storytellers who might want to steer players into some ruin they've spent a week writing up.<br /> <br /> Following that is Beckon the Wandering Wolf, which introduces us properly to Hundred Rivers, the giant wolf V'neef soothed in her youth. Following that is a sidebar that gives us more details on how he works, such as how his Intimacy to the wielder is Minor but can grow with shared positive experiences... and diminish with negative experiences.<br /> <br /> \u200bI wish Hundred Rivers' statblock had been around when I was doing my seafaring game; there was some initial hand-wringing for how I was going to stat out Hunter the Hound of Albada, and this would've been pretty easy to crib.<br /> <br /> \u200bContinuing on, Wolf-and-Dragon Bond, permits the Dragon-Blooded wielder to more easily train Hundred Rivers. I like that this Evocation only awakens if the wielder endures hardship or risks her life to help Hundred Rivers.<br /> <br /> Last of all is Packmate Devotion, which makes Hundred Rivers' devotion sacrosanct; the only thing that'd diminish his bond with the wielder is outright betrayal. Moreover, seeing the wielder suffer decisive damage grants Hundred Rivers extra Initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}